        "```{=latex}\n",
        "\\endgroup\n",
        "```\n",
        "We first inspect missing values across the selected stock-level characteristics, macroeconomic variables, the prediction target, lagged market capitalization, and industry classification. In the current sample, no missing values are observed in these variables, and the cleaning procedure therefore does not reduce the number of observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "As a safeguard and to ensure a consistent preprocessing pipeline, missing values in stock-level characteristics are handled using monthly cross-sectional median imputation. This approach would preserve stock-month observations while relying only on contemporaneous information from the same month. The median is preferred to the mean because it is less sensitive to extreme firm-level observations, which are common in financial data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Macroeconomic variables are common to all firms within a given month and vary only over time. Since no missing macroeconomic values are observed in the current sample, no macro imputation is required. Nevertheless, the preprocessing pipeline applies forward filling if missing macroeconomic values are encountered, so that only previously observed macroeconomic information is used. Backward filling is avoided to prevent look-ahead bias.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, observations with missing excess returns or lagged market capitalization would be dropped if present because `ret_excess` is the prediction target and `mktcap_lag` is required to construct value-weighted portfolio returns."
      ],
