        "After cleaning, the final sample contains `{python} f\"{n_obs_final:,}\"` stock-month observations across `{python} f\"{n_firms_final:,}\"` firms and `{python} n_months_final` months. The missing-value treatment balances data retention with robustness, while the industry recoding keeps the dimensionality of the feature matrix manageable.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1c: Feature matrix construction\n",
        "First, we recode `sic2` into the 10 major SIC divisions to retain broad industry information while keeping the feature space manageable. This reduces the number of industry dummy variables and lowers the risk that sparse industry categories create noisy predictors in the machine learning models."
      ],
      "id": "3a68bdab"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def recode_sic(sic):\n",
        "    if pd.isna(sic):\n",
        "        return \"Other\"\n",
        "    sic = int(sic)\n",
        "    if sic < 10:\n",
        "        return \"Agriculture\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 15:\n",
        "        return \"Mining\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 18:\n",
        "        return \"Construction\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 40:\n",
        "        return \"Manufacturing\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 50:\n",
        "        return \"Transportation\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 52:\n",
        "        return \"Wholesale\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 60:\n",
        "        return \"Retail\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 70:\n",
        "        return \"Finance\"\n",
        "    elif sic < 90:\n",
        "        return \"Services\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        return \"Public Admin\"\n",
        "\n",
        "df[\"sic_division\"] = df[\"sic2\"].apply(recode_sic)"
      ],
      "id": "8c766a28",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Then, we construct the feature matrix using the selected stock characteristics and their interactions with macroeconomic state variables. The feature matrix contains 59 predictors: 10 stock characteristics, 40 characteristic-macro interactions, and 9 industry dummies. \n",
        "\n",
        "The interaction terms allow firm-level return predictability to vary with macroeconomic conditions, consistent with @Gu.2020. One SIC division is omitted as the reference category when constructing industry dummies."
