      "source": [
        "Continuous predictors are standardized using the training sample only. The same transformation is then applied to the validation and test sets, which avoids data leakage from future observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise 2c: Hyperparameter tuning\n",
        "Hyperparameters are tuned using grid search. Each candidate specification is fitted on the training sample and evaluated on the validation sample using RMSE, consistent with the mean squared prediction error objective in @Gu.2020. For Elastic Net, the grid varies the overall penalty strength (`alpha`) and the balance between Lasso and Ridge regularization (`l1_ratio`). For Random Forest, we vary tree depth while keeping the number of trees, feature subsampling rule, and minimum leaf size fixed. This allows us to examine how increasing model complexity affects predictive accuracy while keeping computation feasible.\n"
      ],
      "id": "3968315c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "# elastic net hyperparameter grid\n",
        "en_param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"alpha\": [0.001, 0.01, 0.1],\n",
        "    \"l1_ratio\": [0.2, 0.5, 0.8],\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "en_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for params in [dict(zip(en_param_grid, v)) for v in itertools.product(*en_param_grid.values())]:\n",
        "    model = ElasticNet(\n",
        "        max_iter=5000,\n",
        "        fit_intercept=True,\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "        **params\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "    en_results.append({\n",
        "        **params,\n",
        "        \"train_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_train, model.predict(X_train)),\n",
        "        \"val_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_val, model.predict(X_val))\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "en_results_df = pd.DataFrame(en_results).sort_values(\"val_rmse\")\n",
        "\n",
        "best_en_params = en_results_df.iloc[0][[\"alpha\", \"l1_ratio\"]].to_dict()"
      ],
      "id": "d6221e42",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "# random forest hyperparameter grid\n",
        "rf_param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [50],\n",
        "    \"max_features\": [\"sqrt\"],\n",
