        "The final fitted models are saved to disk using `joblib` to ensure reproducibility and facilitate peer review.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exercise 3\n",
        "### Exercise 3a-c: Predictions and long-short portfolios\n",
        "Using the fitted Elastic Net and Random Forest models from Exercise 2, we generate predicted excess returns for each stock-month observation in the validation and test samples. The test set is only used for final out-of-sample evaluation and is not used for model fitting or hyperparameter selection."
      ],
      "id": "a48186bc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# generate predictions directly from fitted models\n",
        "pred_val_en = final_en.predict(X_val)\n",
        "pred_val_rf = final_rf.predict(X_val)\n",
        "\n",
        "pred_test_en = final_en.predict(X_test)\n",
        "pred_test_rf = final_rf.predict(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "# add predictions to metadata\n",
        "meta_val = meta_val.copy()\n",
        "meta_val[\"pred_en\"] = pred_val_en\n",
        "meta_val[\"pred_rf\"] = pred_val_rf\n",
        "\n",
        "meta_test = meta_test.copy()\n",
        "meta_test[\"pred_en\"] = pred_test_en\n",
        "meta_test[\"pred_rf\"] = pred_test_rf"
      ],
      "id": "f132986a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For each month, stocks are sorted into decile portfolios based on predicted excess returns. Decile 0 contains the lowest predicted returns and decile 9 contains the highest predicted returns. Realized excess returns within each decile are computed as value-weighted averages using `mktcap_lag`."
      ],
      "id": "5d929b77"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def assign_deciles(df, pred_col, decile_col):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Assign stocks to decile portfolios each month based on predicted returns.\n",
        "    Uses ranked predictions to avoid qcut dropping bins when many values are tied.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    df = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    def month_deciles(x):\n",
        "        if x.notna().sum() < 10:\n",
        "            return pd.Series(np.nan, index=x.index)\n",
        "\n",
        "        ranked = x.rank(method=\"first\")\n",
        "        return pd.qcut(ranked, 10, labels=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    df[decile_col] = df.groupby(\"date\")[pred_col].transform(month_deciles)\n",
        "    df[decile_col] = pd.to_numeric(df[decile_col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "meta_val = assign_deciles(meta_val, \"pred_en\", \"decile_en\")\n",
        "meta_val = assign_deciles(meta_val, \"pred_rf\", \"decile_rf\")\n",
        "\n",
        "meta_test = assign_deciles(meta_test, \"pred_en\", \"decile_en\")\n",
        "meta_test = assign_deciles(meta_test, \"pred_rf\", \"decile_rf\")"
      ],
      "id": "ecbe5f45",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The long-short strategy buys the top predicted-return decile and shorts the bottom predicted-return decile. The monthly long-short return is therefore the value-weighted return of decile 9 minus the value-weighted return of decile 0."
      ],
      "id": "4bc29886"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def compute_longshort(df, decile_col):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Compute monthly value-weighted long-short portfolio returns.\n",
        "    Long = top decile (9), Short = bottom decile (0).\n",
        "    Skips months where one of the legs is missing.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for date, group in df.groupby(\"date\"):\n",
        "        group = group.dropna(subset=[decile_col, \"ret_excess\", \"mktcap_lag\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "        long_leg = group[group[decile_col] == 9]\n",
        "        short_leg = group[group[decile_col] == 0]\n",
        "\n",
        "        if len(long_leg) == 0 or len(short_leg) == 0:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "\n",
        "        if long_leg[\"mktcap_lag\"].sum() <= 0 or short_leg[\"mktcap_lag\"].sum() <= 0:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "\n",
        "        long_ret = np.average(long_leg[\"ret_excess\"], weights=long_leg[\"mktcap_lag\"])\n",
        "        short_ret = np.average(short_leg[\"ret_excess\"], weights=short_leg[\"mktcap_lag\"])\n",
        "        ls_ret = long_ret - short_ret\n",
        "\n",
        "        results.append({\n",
        "            \"date\": date,\n",
        "            \"long_ret\": long_ret,\n",
        "            \"short_ret\": short_ret,\n",
        "            \"ls_ret\": ls_ret\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "    out = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if out.empty:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"No valid months found for {decile_col}. \"\n",
        "            f\"Check whether both decile 0 and decile 9 exist in each month.\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    out[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(out[\"date\"])\n",
        "    return out.set_index(\"date\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ls_val_en  = compute_longshort(meta_val,  \"decile_en\")\n",
        "ls_val_rf  = compute_longshort(meta_val,  \"decile_rf\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ls_test_en = compute_longshort(meta_test, \"decile_en\")\n",
        "ls_test_rf = compute_longshort(meta_test, \"decile_rf\")"
      ],
      "id": "8271381b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Exercise 3d: Performance metrics\n",
        "The market benchmark is constructed as the value-weighted average excess return across all stocks in the relevant sample. This makes the benchmark comparable to the long-short portfolio, since both returns are measured in excess of the risk-free rate. CAPM alpha is estimated by regressing the long-short portfolio excess return on the value-weighted market excess return.\n",
        "\n",
        "@tbl-performance reports annualized mean excess returns, Sharpe ratios, CAPM alphas, and alpha t-statistics for the long-short portfolios and the market benchmark. Elastic Net performs consistently across validation and test, with positive annualized returns and Sharpe ratios in both periods. Random Forest performs reasonably in validation but delivers negative test-period performance, suggesting that its predictive signal is less stable out-of-sample. The alpha t-statistics are below conventional significance levels, so the evidence for statistically significant abnormal returns is weak."
      ],
      "id": "6b52e96b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def portfolio_stats(ls_returns, market_returns=None):\n",
        "    r = ls_returns[\"ls_ret\"]\n",
        "    ann_mean = r.mean() * 12\n",
        "    ann_sharpe = r.mean() / r.std() * np.sqrt(12)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if market_returns is not None:\n",
        "        aligned = pd.concat([r, market_returns], axis=1).dropna()\n",
        "        aligned.columns = [\"ls_ret\", \"mkt_excess_ret\"]\n",
        "        X_capm = sm.add_constant(aligned[\"mkt_excess_ret\"])\n",
        "        res = sm.OLS(aligned[\"ls_ret\"], X_capm).fit()\n",
        "        alpha = res.params[\"const\"] * 12\n",
        "        alpha_t = res.tvalues[\"const\"]\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        alpha, alpha_t = np.nan, np.nan\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"ann_mean\": ann_mean,\n",
        "        \"sharpe\": ann_sharpe,\n",
        "        \"alpha\": alpha,\n",
        "        \"alpha_t\": alpha_t\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "def market_stats(market_returns):\n",
        "    r = market_returns.dropna()\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"ann_mean\": r.mean() * 12,\n",
        "        \"sharpe\": r.mean() / r.std() * np.sqrt(12),\n",
        "        \"alpha\": np.nan,\n",
        "        \"alpha_t\": np.nan\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "mkt_val = meta_val.groupby(\"date\").apply(\n",
        "    lambda g: np.average(g[\"ret_excess\"], weights=g[\"mktcap_lag\"])\n",
        ").rename(\"mkt_excess_ret\")\n",
        "\n",
        "mkt_test = meta_test.groupby(\"date\").apply(\n",
        "    lambda g: np.average(g[\"ret_excess\"], weights=g[\"mktcap_lag\"])\n",
        ").rename(\"mkt_excess_ret\")\n",
        "\n",
        "results_3d = [\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Elastic Net\", \"Sample\": \"Validation\", **portfolio_stats(ls_val_en, mkt_val)},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Random Forest\", \"Sample\": \"Validation\", **portfolio_stats(ls_val_rf, mkt_val)},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Market\", \"Sample\": \"Validation\", **market_stats(mkt_val)},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Elastic Net\", \"Sample\": \"Test\", **portfolio_stats(ls_test_en, mkt_test)},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Random Forest\", \"Sample\": \"Test\", **portfolio_stats(ls_test_rf, mkt_test)},\n",
        "    {\"Model\": \"Market\", \"Sample\": \"Test\", **market_stats(mkt_test)},\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "results_3d_df = pd.DataFrame(results_3d)"
      ],
      "id": "27d83b84",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: tbl-performance\n",
        "#| tbl-cap: Annualized long-short portfolio performance and market benchmark\n",
        "Markdown(results_3d_df.round(4).to_markdown(index=False))"
      ],
      "id": "tbl-performance",
      "execution_count": null,
